Found under k326 (destroy worker, 2026-10-31). `ocp destroy` runs no validate() (on purpose, k323: only what destroy reads), and three shapes it reads still go through unchecked -- all exit 0, no Perl error, so nothing says anything went wrong:
1. `name: [prod]`: the server search uses the label value ARRAY(0x...), so an unrecorded server labelled prod is missed while the run says "Cluster destroyed." -- a server can be left billing. validate() refuses a list as name since k305.
2. A worker pool's own `host: [a, b]` becomes one machine named ARRAY(0x...) (k323 covered hosts inside nodes: only).
3. A control plane's `host: [a]` does the same in the control-plane fallback.

Fix: extend k323/k326's up-front check (Destroy::_spec_*_errors) to name and host, in validate()'s words, before the PIN and before anything is touched. A public OCP::Config shape helper (k306) would let destroy stop re-spelling validate()'s lines.

Done = tests for the three: destroy stops with validate()'s line and touches nothing.

